      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "To investigate the implementation of state- and school-mandated physical education (PE) and physical activity policies on students' school-day physical activity behaviors."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Observational, cross-sectional study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Five elementary schools in rural Alabama."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SUBJECTS",
          "content": "Six hundred and eighty-three school-age children."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MEASURES",
          "content": "School-day physical activity behaviors were assessed with pedometer step count, the System for Observing Fitness Instruction Time (SOFIT), and the System for Observing Play and Leisure Activity in Youth (SOPLAY)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "ANALYSIS",
          "content": "Descriptive statistics (means and standard deviations) were used to describe the current health and in-school physical activity behaviors of students."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Students accumulated a daily average of 4079.57 (± 1678.1) and 3473.44 (± 1073.37) steps for boys and girls, respectively, throughout the school day. SOFIT findings indicate that students spent an average of 23.80 ± 5.33 min/d in PE and that 14.33 ± 6.10 min/d were spent in moderate to vigorous physical activity (MVPA). This equates to 59.38% of PE time spent in MVPA. SOPLAY findings showed that recess and before/after school activity was not provided."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "It appears that schools were in compliance with the state-mandated PE policies on paper but not in actuality. Students did not attend PE for 30 min/d. The implementation of PE as the sole physical activity opportunity provides inadequate amounts of physical activity during the school day."
        }
      ]},
